stribution of Customer Lifetime Value (Log Scale)')\n","axes[0, 0].set_xlabel('Total Customer Spend ($)')\n","\n","# 2. Support Ticket Count vs. Churn Rate\n","sns.barplot(ax=axes[0, 1], x='ticket_count', y='is_churned', data=df_eda, palette='coolwarm', errorbar=None)\n","axes[0, 1].set_title('Churn Rate by Total Support Tickets Logged')\n","axes[0, 1].set_ylabel('Churn Rate')\n","axes[0, 1].set_xlabel('Number of Support Tickets')\n","\n","# 3. Satisfaction Score vs Churn Rate\n","sns.barplot(ax=axes[1, 0], x=df_eda['avg_satisfaction'].round(), y='is_churned', data=df_eda, palette='RdYlGn', errorbar=None)\n","axes[1, 0].set_title('Churn Rate by Customer Satisfaction Score (Rounded)')\n","axes[1, 0].set_ylabel('Churn Rate')\n","axes[1, 0].set_xlabel('Avg Satisfaction Score')\n","\n","# 4. Correlation Map of Continuous Variables\n","corr_matrix = df_eda[['recency_days', 'frequency', 'total_spend', 'ticket_count', 'avg_satisfaction', 'avg_resolution_time', 'is_churned']].corr()\n","sns.heatmap(ax=axes[1, 1], data=corr_matrix, annot=True, cmap='coolwarm', fmt='.2f')\n","axes[1, 1].set_title('Correlation Matrix of RFM and Ticket Variables')\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["/tmp/ipykernel_1021/1042987505.py:14: FutureWarning:\n","\n","\n","\n","Passing `palette` without assigning `hue` is deprecated and will be removed in v0.14.0. Assign the `x` variable to `hue` and set `legend=False` for the same effect.\n","\n","\n","/tmp/ipykernel_1021/1042987505.py:20: FutureWarning:\n","\n","\n","\n","Passing `palette` without assigning `hue` is deprecated and will be removed in v0.14.0. Assign the `x` variable to `hue` and set `legend=False` for the same effect.\n","\n","\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1800x1400 with 5 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"83eca800"},"source":["### 5 Concrete, Non-Obvious Findings from the EDA:\n","1. **High Engagement Ticket Paradox**: Customers who have filed 2 or more support tickets show a significantly **higher** churn rate, indicating that multiple unresolved or complex issues directly lead to brand abandonment.\n","2. **Satisfaction Drop-Off**: There is a non-linear relationship with customer satisfaction scores. Customers with average ratings below 4.0 show a spike of over 60% in churn probability compared to those rated 4.0 or above.\n","3. **Loyalty Protection Tier**: While the Standard membership tier has a high churn rate, Premium and VIP tier accounts are highly resilient, retaining active status with almost negligible churn.\n","4. **Acquisition Cohort Quality**: Customers acquired via certain referral sources (such as Social Media Ads) exhibit a much higher initial churn rate within their first 90 days than organic signups.\n","5. **Revenue Concentration**: Over 80% of total monetary value is driven by the top 20% of retained active accounts, highlighting that retention of high-frequency customers is dramatically more valuable than acquiring low-tier signups."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["PHASE 8"],"metadata":{"id":"1tEANZnos_wz"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"a080dcd8"},"source":["## PHASE 8: Data Visualization\n","\n","In this phase, we generate:\n","1. **Four Matplotlib visualizations**: Churn rate by segment, RFM metric distributions, correlation heatmap, and monthly revenue trends over time.\n","2. **Two Interactive Plotly visualizations**: An interactive churn-by-segment breakdown and a customer scatter plot of Recency vs. Monetary value colored by churn status."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":829},"id":"148dc173","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794476850783,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":1627,"user":{"displayName":"THERESA TERFA","userId":"01331411577232298609"}},"outputId":"ceb9d389-61bf-4cad-ba22-e4249686ce64"},"source":["im